FOOTNOTE 7: Dollars $116,001-$173,688 realized in FY2021 reserves from not rolling over line items as
indicated in Footnote 12 from FY2020 shall be added to the Fire Department budget.
FOOTNOTE 3: The first $17,500 realized in FY2021 reserves from not rolling over line items as indicated in
Footnote 12 from FY2020 shall be added to the Miscellaneous Department to be appropriated to Safe
Harbor.
FOOTNOTE 4: Dollars $17,501-$32,501 realized in FY2021 reserves from not rolling over line items as
indicated in Footnote 12 from FY2020 shall be added to the Miscellaneous Department to be appropriated
to Animal Shelter.
FOOTNOTE 5: Dollars $32,501-$57,501 realized in FY2021 reserves from not rolling over line items as
indicated in Footnote 12 from FY2020 shall be added to the Miscellaneous Department to be appropriated
to Laramie County Senior Services.
FOOTNOTE 6: Dollars $57,501-$116,001 realized in FY2021 reserves from not rolling over line items as
indicated in Footnote 12 from FY2020 shall be added to the Miscellaneous Department to be appropriated
to Animal Control.
General Fund
FOOTNOTE 8: Consistent with Senate Enrolled Act 1 (SEA 1) of the Wyoming Legislature’s 2020 Special
Session, Section 1(b)(iii) “economic development projects”-the first $51,328.26 of federal CARES Act dollars
the City of Cheyenne receives after reimbursement to the City for direct COVID-19 related expenditures
pursuant to SEA 1 shall be appropriated to the Downtown Development Authority for the following
expenditures:  Emergency Microgrants - $51,328.26.
FOOTNOTE 9: Consistent with Senate Enrolled Act 1 (SEA 1) of the Wyoming Legislature’s 2020 Special
Session, Sections 1(b)(i)&(iv)-the $51,328.27th cent and dollar through the $196,681.27th cent and dollar
of federal CARES Act funds the City of Cheyenne receives after reimbursement to the City for direct COVID-
19 related expenditures pursuant to SEA 1 shall be appropriated to the City/County Health Department for
expenditures consistent with federal law and SEA 1. If this dollar amount exceeds the eligible expenditures
of the City/County Health Department, the remaining next dollar on will then be prioritized to the intent of
Footnote 10.
FOOTNOTE 10: Consistent with Senate Enrolled Act 1 (SEA 1) of the Wyoming Legislature’s 2020 Special
Session, Section 1(b)-the $196,681.28th cent and dollar through the $311,681.28th cent and dollar of
federal CARES Act funds the City of Cheyenne receives after reimbursement to the City for direct COVID-19
related expenditures pursuant to SEA 1 shall be appropriated to the Alcohol Receiving Center for
expenditures consistent with federal law and SEA 1. If this dollar amount exceeds the eligible expenditures
of the Alcohol Receiving Center, the remaining next dollar on will then be prioritized to the intent of
Footnote 11.
FOOTNOTE 11: Consistent with Senate Enrolled Act 1 (SEA 1) of the Wyoming Legislature’s 2020 Special
Session, Section 1(b)(iv), any CARES Act dollars received by the City of Cheyenne after reimbursement to
the City for direct COVID-19 related expenditures through SEA 1 or otherwise, not spent as set forth in
footnotes 10, 11, 12 shall next be appropriated to eligible expenditures budgeted to be funded by reserves
in FY2021. Said expenditures are related to the $775,000 designated for the Civic Center and the $260,000
Minimum Revenue Guarantee for the Airport.
FOOTNOTE 12: There are General Fund line items historically rolled over each fiscal year that will not be
rolled over in FY 2021, either in part or in total, and will instead be used to fund $17,500 for Safe Harbor,
$15,000 for the Cheyenne Animal Shelter for shelter services, $25,000 for Laramie County Senior Services,
and $58,500 for the Cheyenne Animal Shelter for animal control services. An additional $57,687 will be
used to fund the Fire Department. These rollover line items total $132,685 and include $50,000 in Belvoir
Ranch Planning/Development (001-21-2113-40-43906); $13,216 in Right of Way Purchases/Professional
Fees (001-21-2113-40-43908); $56,196 in Municipal Building Major Replacements (001-21-2113-40-86935)
and $13,273 in Capital Improvement Expenses (001-21-2113-40-32107). The remaining funds in the
amount of $35,602 will be transferred from the Miscellaneous Department insurance line item as a result
of a lower property, liability and crime coverage rate increase than what was projected.
FOOTNOTE 13: Move $61,998 from the Miscellaneous Department insurance line item to the Community
Recreation and Events Aquatics Division as a result of a lower property, liability and crime coverage
insurance rate increase than was projected.
